WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 size:84% position:42%
-Can you talk about --
I know you have two new

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
hopefully "initiatives"
is the right word,

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:07.841
basically the Climate Realit
Project and climate tracing.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:11.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, thank you. Well,
the Climate Reality Projec

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:16.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a project that I starte
back in 2006

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.484 line:92%
with all of the profits from

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
the movie and book
"An Inconvenient Truth."

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.091
And right now, we're in
the middle of our 44th training,

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is the first
virtual training,

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.630 line:92%
and I was so happy that 14--

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than 14,000 people
applied to join.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.635 line:92%
We couldn't handle that many

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we don't have
enough mentors

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.673 line:92%
to do that big a group yet

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.610 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But 10,000 signed up.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.813 size:84% position:42%
We're in the sixth day
of a nine-day training.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:50.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in the nature
of these virtual trainings

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
you avoid what they call
"Zoom fatigue"

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
by doing it two hours a day,
basically.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a real thing, and --
-I believe it.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:05.298
-Yeah. And so, it's going
extremely well. Thank you.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have people
from 130 countries,

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we give them the facts
about the science,

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
the causes, the impacts,
the solutions,

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.276
and we give them advocacy
and communication skills

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
even better than what
most of them already have.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:23.616
And you asked, also, about
the climate trace initiative

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
This is a new coalition

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:34.027
that is made up of nine tech
organizations and companies.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.296 line:92%
A lot of brilliant young peopl

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
engaged in
artificial intelligence

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.133 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and machine learning.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our goal is to launch
next June.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll have a hard launch
at the beginning of the year

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
But by next June,
we will have a report

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:57.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
on every significant
greenhouse gas emissions

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.352 size:88% position:44% line:92%
anywhere in the world --

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
how much,
who's responsible for it -

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we'll update it
every six hours.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:08.294 size:88% position:44%
And the point is to make
these folks accountable

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for the first time.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:10.997 line:92%
There are a lot of governments

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
that really have a hard time
understanding

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
where their own greenhouse
gas emissions are coming from.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.405
There are a lot of companies
that want their supply chain

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
to scrub out
the global warming pollution

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are a lot of activists
that want to know where
it's coming from.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:29.215
And there are a lot of investors
who want to take their money

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of companies
that are busy

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
at destroying the future
of human civilization

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.358
and put it into companies that
are facilitating a transitio

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:42.996
to a cleaner and more prosperous
and sustainable world.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.697 line:92%
-You mentioned Zoom fatigue.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
Having been a candidate
for the presidency,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.871
can you imagine what it must
be like for Joe Biden right now,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
having to basically campaign
from his home?

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be so different
from what you experienced.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.013 line:92%
-Well, it's very different

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:05.051
We haven't seen a campaign
like this one geographically

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.320 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for a long, long time,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
since before the days
of television.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that's he's
handling it extremely well

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.895 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know, I'm for him.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you can take my remark
with a grain of salt.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I really think
he's doing extremely well.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
And most people
seem to share that view.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:32.011 size:88% position:44%
-You -- He maybe was not
the greenest candidate

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
when there was
a large debate field.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yet, he seems to be taking
the environment very seriously

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.086 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on his platform now.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.055 line:92%
Are you -- You know, obviously

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:45.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
considering how you feel
about it as an issue,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.926 line:92%
are you optimistic so far

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
how he would address it
as the President?

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. And to put
your comment in perspective,

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's true that
there were other candidates,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Jay Inslee, prominently
and others, as well,

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:03.943
who had maybe a bolder climate
agenda during the primaries,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
but if you look at Joe Biden's
plan during the primaries,

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:13.152
it was miles ahead of what w
have seen in any previous cycle.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:20.493
And, wisely, he has adopte
some of the best proposals

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.028 line:92%
from his primary opponents

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
and fully integrated them
into his new plan.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have enjoyed my conversation
with him

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:32.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
since Joe Biden
secured the nomination.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very happy with
what he has proposed.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are always a few thing
that I would,

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
do a little differently,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.714 line:92%
go a little farther and faster

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, honestly,
it is a great platform,

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think it's getting
rave reviews

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:51.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
from most all the folks
who really care about
the climate crisis.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, Joe Biden
is far ahead in the polls,

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.730 size:81% position:41%
but we should still be
very worried, right?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can't just rest
on our laurels here

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be happy with a 15-point
lead in a July poll.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.506 line:92%
-Well, I can confirm that, yes

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:11.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
The actual votes are what
determine the winner.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.914 size:84% position:42% line:92%
His lead is a good one.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.549 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But after the experience

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
supporters of the nominee
four years ago had

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
watching a poll lead
not quite as large as this one

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
but pretty big
just sort of disappear,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:29.262 size:84% position:42%
everybody kind of says,
"Well, wait a minute.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not taking anything
for granted."

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would like to quote
the great departed John Lewis.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a dear friend
and such a great champion.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, also, a climate champion,
by the way.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:49.115
He and I introduced the very
first environmental justice bill

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
30 years ago.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when he crossed
the Edmund Pettus Bridge

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the very last time
last year --

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
people knew that
he had pancreatic cancer,

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was
an emotional occasion --

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.696 line:92%
he got to the other side.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.165
And I was watching the interview
on television.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:09.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got kind of emotiona
hearing him say --

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:16.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "We've got to vot
like we've never voted before.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:20.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I hope everybody
takes that message to hear

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:23.316 size:75% position:38%
because this will be
a turnout election.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:26.285 line:92%
Trump supporters will turn out

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.255 line:92%
And the supporters of Bide

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:32.458 size:84% position:42%
just need to turn out
in even larger numbers.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:36.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kind of think that's the
direction it's headed in
right now.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:40.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
But nobody should take
a single vote for granted.

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for your time.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a pleasure
speaking with you.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And hopefully, next time
will be in person.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:48.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hope so, too. Thanks, Seth.
Keep up the great work.

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.309 line:92%
-All right. All the best.

